{"name":"Spilt Milk","hex":"#f4f4d1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spilt milk","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something that cannot be undone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spilt_milk"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spilt Milk (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Spilt Milk is a 2024 Irish film, directed by Brian Durnin and written by Cara Loftus. It stars Cillian Sullivan, Naoise Kelly, Danielle Galligan, Laurence O'Fuarain, and Lewis Brophy. It premiered at the Tallinn Black Nights Film Festival in 2024."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6e/Spilt_Milk_2024_film_poster.webp/330px-Spilt_Milk_2024_film_poster.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spilt_Milk_(film)","wikidata":"Q131842546"},{"title":"Spilt Milk (Jellyfish album)","blocks":[{"text":"Spilt Milk is the second and final studio album by American rock band Jellyfish, released on February 9, 1993, by Charisma Records. It features a harsher and more ornate sound than their previous, Bellybutton (1990). As with Bellybutton, Spilt Milk was written and co-produced by founding members Andy Sturmer and Roger Manning. Albhy Galuten and Jack Joseph Puig also returned as producers."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/51/Spilt_Milk_albumcover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spilt_Milk_(Jellyfish_album)","wikidata":"Q7577341"},{"title":"Spilt","blocks":[{"text":"Spilt are a British rock band from Runcorn, England. Formed in 2016, the band consists of Morgan \"Mo\" Molyneux Ben Cunliffe (bass), and Josh Cunningham (drums)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Spilt_new_logo.png/330px-Spilt_new_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spilt","wikidata":"Q65043322"}],"ima